      "role": "user",
      "content": "here is the data from hop 4 and 5. it seems to spike right at the transition between the local gateway and the provider edge. \n\ntraceroute to 194.24.x.x:\n1  192.168.1.1  0.423 ms  0.398 ms  0.411 ms\n2  10.0.45.1  2.105 ms  2.088 ms  2.150 ms\n3  172.16.0.5  12.450 ms  15.902 ms  14.112 ms\n4  194.24.12.1  45.221 ms  112.890 ms  48.331 ms\n5  194.24.12.2  52.110 ms  145.332 ms  51.980 ms\n6  78.x.x.x  32.441 ms  31.992 ms  32.105 ms\n\nping stats:\nDestination: 194.24.12.2\nStatistics:\n    Packets: Sent = 50, Received = 46, Lost = 4 (8% loss)\n    Approximate round trip times in milli-seconds:\n    Minimum = 44ms, Maximum = 152ms, Average = 58ms\n\nit's not constant, just happens in bursts. any idea what's causing that jump at hop 4?",
